course: dictionary
lesson: 4271
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Graze is one of them. It can be about animals eating, about skin getting scraped, or about touching something lightly. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Dugongs graze on sea grass like underwater cows.» Here graze is something animals do. Ask yourself: who is grazing, and what are they eating? Cows, dugongs and sheep all eat grass, so graze means to eat grass slowly, as grazing animals do.
explain: «For a small cut or graze, wash it with clean water.» Now graze is a thing you can get. The words cut, wash and cover tell you it is a small hurt on your skin. When you are not sure which meaning fits, put your idea into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Graze can be a verb (graze, grazes, grazed, grazing) or a noun (graze, grazes).
fact: As a verb, to graze means animals like cows, sheep and horses eat grass in a field.
fact: As a verb, to graze your skin means to scrape it a little, like a knee when you fall.
fact: As a noun, a graze is that small scrape on your skin.
fact: To graze can also mean to touch something lightly as you pass it.
exercise: «Dugongs graze on sea grass like underwater cows.» What does graze mean here? | *To eat grass slowly, as animals do | To scrape your skin | To swim very fast | To shout loudly
exercise: «For a small cut or graze, wash it with clean water.» What is a graze in this sentence? | A cow in a field | A plaster | *A small scrape on the skin | A tall tree
exercise: Mia says, «I grazed my knee on the path.» What does grazed mean? | Stroked gently | *Scraped a little | Painted | Ate grass
test: Six cows graze in a field. Two leave the field. How many cows are still grazing? | 8 | *4 | 2 | 6
test: «A boy in Leeds did not clean a graze from the playground.» What should you do with a graze to keep it safe? | *Clean it with water and cover it | Rub dirt into it | Ignore it, because it always goes away | Leave it dirty
exam: «The bird's wing grazed the top of the wall as it flew past.» Which meaning of graze fits here? | *To touch lightly as you pass | To eat grass | To scrape your skin badly | To run very fast
